From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slothfulchat <patches@slothfulchat.invalid>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 03:01:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] web-app: onboarding in four steps, with up to three relays

The welcome screen becomes a short flow:

1. Welcome: what the app is (four selling points, a "What's different"
   link) and, on instances built with analytics, an explicit Share / Don't
   share choice instead of the opt-out checkbox. Nothing is preselected;
   Next waits for the choice, and only then sends the top-of-funnel event,
   so a "Don't share" never lets it (or anything held before it) out.
   Instances without analytics say they collect none.
2. Bridge: This device / Hosted / Custom tiles over the runtime's bridge
   list (window.__slothfulchatBridge gains local, options, probe, use,
   normalize). The hosted dropdown shows each operator's description and a
   live ping; it is a native popover positioned under its button, so it
   never stretches or gets clipped by the dialog's scroll area (in-place
   fallback without popover support). Switching reloads, like the bridge
   dialog always did; a sessionStorage marker returns to step 3.
3. Profile kind: new profile, "I already have a profile" (backup import,
   which replaces the alternative-setups dialog), or a madmail server, and
   scanning an invite or relay QR.
4. New profile: nothing preselected. "Decide for me" is a disabled
   placeholder for an automatic choice; "Choose relays myself" opens the
   relay picker of desktop/1023 in a new multi-select mode (up to three,
   three recommended) that also leads to a classic email account, with its
   trade-offs and a hosted-bridge warning. The profile is created on the
   first chatmail relay ("Main", "Make main" changes it): a classic
   provider as the main transport would send everything through a
   rate-limited account. The other relays are added once the profile
   exists, in the background, and any that fail are reported together.
   Every picked relay is pinged, typed and scanned ones included; a QR
   button next to the picker adds a scanned relay. A scanned dcaccount: QR
   no longer pins the server, it joins the list (madmail QRs still pin).
   After an invite, the relays of its a= addresses that are in the
   directory are offered. The consent covers all picked relays and opens a
   list of their privacy policies.

The manual classic-email login and the "other servers" dialog leave the
onboarding: a classic account is now one of the picked relays. The
onboarding, relay-picker and classic-email dialogs join desktop/1009's
full-screen-on-phones list. Strings live in packages/web-app/fork-strings.json.
